01:06:19,840 --> 01:06:21,680
so something I haven't really called out yet,
所以有件事我还没真正说出来呢，

1658
01:06:21,680 --> 01:06:23,360
the inner layers are higher
内层更高

1659
01:06:23,360 --> 01:06:24,880
because of the way we wrap them.
由于我们包装它们的方式。

1660
01:06:24,880 --> 01:06:28,080
So this innermost layer, highest layer of abstraction,
所以这最内层，最高层的抽象，

1661
01:06:28,080 --> 01:06:30,560
we think about people inside the building.
我们考虑大楼内的人员。

1662
01:06:31,280 --> 01:06:33,120
Alice is the person inside the building,
爱丽丝是楼里的那个人，

1663
01:06:33,120 --> 01:06:34,800
Bob is the person inside the building,
鲍勃是楼里的那个人，

1664
01:06:34,800 --> 01:06:37,040
but it could have been other people inside the building.
但大楼里可能还有其他人。

1665
01:06:37,040 --> 01:06:39,440
Maybe there's another person in the Bob building.
鲍勃大楼里可能还有另一个人。

1666
01:06:39,440 --> 01:06:42,640
So also the CEO could have gone to them as well.
所以CEO本也可以去找他们。

1667
01:06:42,640 --> 01:06:45,200
So that's why we need multiple addressing schemes
这就是为什么我们需要多种寻址方案的原因。

1668
01:06:45,200 --> 01:06:48,000
working at different layers of abstraction.
在不同抽象层级上工作。

1669
01:06:50,240 --> 01:06:52,800
Okay, thoughts before I keep going?
好的，在我继续之前有什么想法吗？

1670
01:06:53,280 --> 01:06:55,200
Okay, almost done.
好的，快完成了。

1671
01:06:55,200 --> 01:06:58,720
So what we actually just saw also tells us
所以我们刚才实际看到的也告诉我们

1672
01:06:58,720 --> 01:07:02,720
what layers each machine has to understand.
每台机器需要理解哪些层次。

1673
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:04,560
So let's think about the end hosts.
那么让我们来思考一下终端主机。

1674
01:07:04,560 --> 01:07:06,400
What do the end hosts have to think about?
终端主机需要考虑什么？

1675
01:07:06,400 --> 01:07:09,760
Turns out the end hosts have to think about everything
到头来，终端主机必须考虑所有事情。

1676
01:07:09,760 --> 01:07:12,800
because the end host has to think about the original packet
因为终端主机必须考虑原始数据包

1677
01:07:12,800 --> 01:07:14,960
and then the end host has to wrap it
然后终端主机必须将其封装起来

1678
01:07:14,960 --> 01:07:17,360
all the way down to layer one,
一直向下到第一层，

1679
01:07:17,360 --> 01:07:20,560
where it becomes ones and zeros and is sent on the wire.
在那里它变成了一串零和一，并通过线路发送出去。

1680
01:07:20,640 --> 01:07:23,680
So if you're the end host, like you're Alice or you're Bob,
所以如果你是终端主机，比如你是爱丽丝或者你是鲍勃，

1681
01:07:23,680 --> 01:07:27,280
your computer has to understand all seven layers.
你的电脑必须理解所有七层。

1682
01:07:27,280 --> 01:07:29,520
You start at layer seven with the message
你从第七层开始接收消息

1683
01:07:29,520 --> 01:07:32,320
and you wrap headers around and around and around
而你一遍又一遍地包裹着标题

1684
01:07:32,320 --> 01:07:35,680
all the way until you get that nested packet
一直深入直到你找到那个嵌套的数据包

1685
01:07:35,680 --> 01:07:37,280
that can get sent along the wire.
这可以沿着线路发送。

1686
01:07:38,080 --> 01:07:40,320
And likewise, at the very end,
同样地，在最终时刻，

1687
01:07:40,320 --> 01:07:41,920
when you reach the destination,
当你到达目的地时，

1688
01:07:41,920 --> 01:07:46,160
they also have to take the packet, unwrap, unwrap, unwrap, unwrap,
他们还得拿起包裹，拆开，拆开，拆开，拆开，

1689
01:07:46,160 --> 01:07:48,080
before they can get the final packet
在他们拿到最终的数据包之前

1690
01:07:48,480 --> 01:07:50,400
with none of the headers attached.
没有任何头文件附加。

1691
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:52,080
So basically the punchline is,
所以基本上笑点就是，

1692
01:07:52,080 --> 01:07:54,480
you'll notice that the end hosts had to understand
你会注意到终端主机必须理解

1693
01:07:54,480 --> 01:07:56,800
all of the layers of abstraction.
所有的抽象层。

1694
01:07:56,800 --> 01:07:59,840
So they have to have code for all five layers.
所以他们必须拥有所有五层的代码。

1695
01:07:59,840 --> 01:08:02,800
By contrast, think about the routers.
相比之下，想想路由器。

1696
01:08:02,800 --> 01:08:05,200
Did the routers ever like open the envelope
路由器们曾经喜欢打开信封吗

1697
01:08:05,200 --> 01:08:07,040
to look at the message inside?
查看里面的信息？

1698
01:08:07,040 --> 01:08:08,800
No, not really.
不，并不是。

1699
01:08:08,800 --> 01:08:11,280
Did they have to understand what was on the envelope
他们必须理解信封上写的是什么吗

1700
01:08:11,280 --> 01:08:13,680
and understand who Alice and Bob were?
并且了解爱丽丝和鲍勃是谁吗？

1701
01:08:13,680 --> 01:08:15,280
No, not really.
不，不完全是。

1702
01:08:15,280 --> 01:08:16,880
What did the routers have to do?
路由器需要做什么？

1703
01:08:16,880 --> 01:08:19,439
They had to unwrap their outermost header,
他们不得不解开他们最外层的头巾，

1704
01:08:19,439 --> 01:08:22,240
look inside to see who the final destination is,
看看里面，最终目的地是谁。

1705
01:08:22,240 --> 01:08:25,520
and then wrap a header to send it to the next top.
然后包装一个标头发送到下一个顶部。

1706
01:08:25,520 --> 01:08:26,640
That's it.
就这样。

1707
01:08:26,640 --> 01:08:29,680
So in other words, the routers only care about layers
换句话说，路由器只关心层

1708
01:08:29,680 --> 01:08:30,880
one, two, and three.
一、二、和三。

1709
01:08:30,880 --> 01:08:32,880
They start at one because everyone starts at one
他们从一做起，因为每个人都从一做起

1710
01:08:32,880 --> 01:08:36,080
with all the packet headers sent along the wire.
随着所有数据包头部一并通过线路发送。

1711
01:08:36,080 --> 01:08:38,880
They unwrap their layer, which is layer two,
他们解开他们的那一层，也就是第二层，

1712
01:08:38,880 --> 01:08:42,880
exposing the layer three destination.
暴露第三层目的地。

1713
01:08:42,880 --> 01:08:44,479
That's the final destination.
那就是最终目的地。

1714
01:08:44,479 --> 01:08:47,279
I read that, and I think, I can't get to four, five, six,
我读到那个，我想，我无法达到四，五，六，

1715
01:08:47,279 --> 01:08:48,479
Bob Street, but you know who can?
鲍勃街，但你知道谁能吗？

1716
01:08:48,479 --> 01:08:50,080
It's my buddy next door.
是我隔壁的哥们儿。

1717
01:08:50,080 --> 01:08:52,880
So then I'll wrap another link layer header
那么我再封装一个链路层头部

1718
01:08:52,880 --> 01:08:54,880
and then send it to my hub next door.
然后把它送到我隔壁的集线器。

1719
01:08:54,880 --> 01:08:56,479
So that's something we'll see in just a bit.
所以我们稍后就会看到这一点。

1720
01:08:56,479 --> 01:08:59,279
Basically, the punchline is end hosts have to understand
基本上，笑点在于终端主机必须理解

1721
01:08:59,279 --> 01:09:02,479
all the layers, whereas routers only have to make their way
所有的层，而路由器只需要打通它们的路径

1722
01:09:02,479 --> 01:09:05,279
up to layer three, and they don't really care about
直到第三层，而他们并不真正关心

1723
01:09:05,279 --> 01:09:07,279
what's inside beyond that.
那里面还有什么。

1724
01:09:07,279 --> 01:09:09,279
So from their perspective, you get to layer three.
所以从他们的角度来看，你到达了第三层。

1725
01:09:09,279 --> 01:09:12,080
Everything beyond that is just payload gibberish.
除此之外的一切都只是载荷乱码。

1726
01:09:13,080 --> 01:09:15,080
I don't care what the message is.
我不在乎信息是什么。

1727
01:09:15,080 --> 01:09:17,080
That's for the end host to decide.
这得由最终主机来决定。

1728
01:09:17,080 --> 01:09:20,080
So what that means is routers don't care about reliability.
所以这意味着路由器并不关心可靠性。

1729
01:09:20,080 --> 01:09:22,080
They don't care about the application data.
他们不在乎应用程序数据。

1730
01:09:22,080 --> 01:09:26,080
They just care about these bottom three layers.
他们只关心这三个底层。

1731
01:09:26,080 --> 01:09:28,080
Okay.
好的。

1732
01:09:28,080 --> 01:09:30,080
Here's a picture of what I just talked about.
这是我刚才提到的图片。

1733
01:09:30,080 --> 01:09:32,080
So I started the very top message.
所以我开始了最顶部的消息。

1734
01:09:32,080 --> 01:09:33,080
What do I do?
我该怎么办？

1735
01:09:33,080 --> 01:09:35,080
I wrap it in layer four.
我把它包在第四层。

1736
01:09:35,080 --> 01:09:37,080
I wrap it in layer three, layer two.
我用三层包裹，再用两层。

1737
01:09:37,080 --> 01:09:41,080
Then I convert it to bits and I send it across the wire.
然后我将其转换为比特并通过线路发送出去。

1738
01:09:41,080 --> 01:09:42,080
Now I get to the router.
现在我来到路由器这里。

1739
01:09:42,080 --> 01:09:46,080
And just like we talked about, the router doesn't care that this says potato.
正如我们之前讨论的，路由器并不在乎这里写的是土豆。

1740
01:09:46,080 --> 01:09:48,080
The router is never going to read that.
路由器永远不会读取那个。

1741
01:09:48,080 --> 01:09:51,080
From the router's perspective, this could be any word or any message.
从路由器的角度来看，这可以是任何词语或任何消息。

1742
01:09:51,080 --> 01:09:52,080
It doesn't matter.
没关系。

1743
01:09:52,080 --> 01:09:56,080
But the router does care about unwrapping this outermost header.
但路由器确实关心解封这最外层的头部。

1744
01:09:56,080 --> 01:09:57,080
So I receive the bits.
于是我接收这些比特。

1745
01:09:57,080 --> 01:09:59,080
I parse them to understand what they mean.
我解析它们以理解其含义。

1746
01:09:59,080 --> 01:10:04,080
I unwrap this layer two header, revealing the layer three header inside,
我解开这层二层头部，露出里面的三层头部，

1747
01:10:04,080 --> 01:10:07,080
which remember that tells me where the final destination is.
这提醒了我最终目的地在哪里。

1748
01:10:07,080 --> 01:10:10,080
And then I wrap another layer two header.
然后我再封装一层二层头部。

1749
01:10:10,080 --> 01:10:15,080
I wrap another layer one header or, you know, convert it to ones and zeros.
我再包裹一层头部，或者，你知道的，把它转换成零和一。

1750
01:10:15,080 --> 01:10:18,080
Then I send it across over here and this router does the same thing.
然后我把它发送到这里，而这个路由器也做同样的事情。

1751
01:10:18,080 --> 01:10:20,080
Unwrapped layers one and two.
已解开第一层和第二层。

1752
01:10:20,080 --> 01:10:23,080
I read layer three to understand where this packet is going.
我阅读第三层以了解这个数据包的去向。

1753
01:10:23,080 --> 01:10:27,080
And then I pass this back down to layer two, add a new header,
然后我将其传回第二层，添加一个新的头部，

1754
01:10:27,080 --> 01:10:31,080
pass it on to layer one, add a new header and send it over.
传递给第一层，添加新标头并发送出去。

1755
01:10:31,080 --> 01:10:34,080
Maybe another way of putting that is once I get here to layer three,
也许另一种表达方式是，一旦我抵达这里进入第三层，

1756
01:10:34,080 --> 01:10:39,080
all this stuff inside blue and purple is complete payload gibberish.
蓝色和紫色内部的所有这些东西都是完整的载荷乱码。

1757
01:10:39,080 --> 01:10:40,080
I don't care what it is.
我不在乎那是什么。

1758
01:10:40,080 --> 01:10:42,080
It's just a bunch of ones and zeros.
这不过是一堆零和一而已。

1759
01:10:42,080 --> 01:10:43,080
I don't know how to read them.
我不知道怎么读它们。

1760
01:10:43,080 --> 01:10:45,080
I don't care what they say.
我才不在乎他们说什么。

1761
01:10:45,080 --> 01:10:49,080
I just care about this layer three header to figure out where the packet is going next.
我只关心这个三层头，以确定数据包下一步的去向。

1762
01:10:49,080 --> 01:10:56,080
I wrap a new layer two header to my next top and then I send the bits across the wire.
我在我的下一个顶部包裹一个新的第二层头部，然后通过线路发送这些比特。

1763
01:10:56,080 --> 01:11:00,080
And once I reach the end, the end host does care about potato.
而一旦我抵达终点，终点宿主确实在意土豆。

1764
01:11:00,080 --> 01:11:02,080
The end host is the one trying to receive this message.
终端主机是试图接收此消息的那一方。

1765
01:11:02,080 --> 01:11:07,080
So the end host will pass the packet all the way back up unwrapped unwrapped unwrapped.
所以终端主机会将数据包一路向上传递，层层解封层层解封层层解封。

1766
01:11:07,080 --> 01:11:09,080
And I get the original message back.
而我收到了原始信息。

1767
01:11:09,080 --> 01:11:13,080
So once I add routers into the picture, this is what it looks like.
所以一旦我把路由器加入画面，情况就变成了这样。

1768
01:11:13,080 --> 01:11:15,080
End host understand all seven layers.
终端主机理解所有七层。

1769
01:11:15,080 --> 01:11:20,080
Routers only understand the first three.
路由器仅理解前三个。

1770
01:11:20,080 --> 01:11:21,080
Okay.
好的。

1771
01:11:21,080 --> 01:11:22,080
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

1772
01:11:22,080 --> 01:11:26,080
Here's a cartoon arrow showing you the path that the packets took.
这是一支卡通箭头，展示数据包所经过的路径。

1773
01:11:26,080 --> 01:11:29,080
I went down the stack here and then at every router,
我顺着堆栈往下走，然后在每一个路由器处，

1774
01:11:29,080 --> 01:11:34,080
it went up the stack unwrapped to see where the final destination is.
它沿着堆栈向上展开，以查看最终目的地是哪里。

1775
01:11:34,080 --> 01:11:38,080
And then go back down, wrap some more headers to tell me where the packet is going next.
然后再往下走，多封装几层头部来告诉我数据包接下来要去哪里。

1776
01:11:38,080 --> 01:11:41,080
Hop over here, go up, go down, up over here,
跳过来，上去，下来，这边上去，

1777
01:11:41,080 --> 01:11:45,080
travel all the way up the stack to reach the final destination.
一路向上遍历整个堆栈，直至抵达最终目的地。

1778
01:11:45,080 --> 01:11:50,080
So this kind of pattern is what packets do as they travel through the internet.
所以这种模式就是数据包在互联网中传输时的行为方式。

1779
01:11:50,080 --> 01:11:54,080
Packets, headers get unwrapped and wrapped over and over again.
数据包、报头被一遍又一遍地解封与封装。

1780
01:11:54,080 --> 01:11:58,080
But these higher layer headers always stay the same.
但这些更高层的头部始终保持不变。

1781
01:11:58,080 --> 01:11:59,080
Okay.
好的。

1782
01:11:59,080 --> 01:12:02,080
So as mentioned earlier, you saw this before with post offices,
正如之前提到的，你之前在邮局见过这种情况，

1783
01:12:02,080 --> 01:12:04,080
but now I'm going to show it to you in computer form.
但现在我要以电脑形式向你展示它。

1784
01:12:04,080 --> 01:12:08,080
So the layer two headers, what addresses are they thinking about?
那么第二层头部，它们考虑的是哪些地址呢？

1785
01:12:08,080 --> 01:12:11,080
They're thinking in terms of the intermediate routers.
他们正在考虑中间路由器的问题。

1786
01:12:11,080 --> 01:12:13,080
I'm router two.
我是路由器二。

1787
01:12:13,080 --> 01:12:17,080
The next hop is router number five is router five, the final destination.
下一跳是路由器五号是路由器五，最终目的地。

1788
01:12:17,080 --> 01:12:22,080
Probably not, but router five will get this packet closer to where it needs to go.
可能不会，但路由器五会让这个数据包更接近它需要去的地方。

1789
01:12:22,080 --> 01:12:23,080
And I'm router two.
而我是路由器二。

1790
01:12:23,080 --> 01:12:31,080
So these are intermediate routers that forward the packet hop by hop as they approach the final destination.
所以这些是中间路由器，它们在数据包接近最终目的地时逐跳转发。

1791
01:12:31,080 --> 01:12:34,080
Layer three, this is actually the real final destination.
第三层，这实际上才是真正的最终目的地。

1792
01:12:34,080 --> 01:12:36,080
Alice's computer, Bob's computer.
爱丽丝的电脑，鲍勃的电脑。

1793
01:12:36,080 --> 01:12:40,080
These are the actual final destinations and they never change.
这些是真正的最终目的地，它们永不改变。

1794
01:12:40,080 --> 01:12:45,080
As the packet travels across the network, it's always from Alice, it's always to Bob.
数据包在网络中穿行时，始终发自爱丽丝，终至鲍勃。

1795
01:12:45,080 --> 01:12:48,080
This outer one is where the intermediate hops change.
这个外层的是中间跳变的地方。

1796
01:12:48,080 --> 01:12:51,080
And then finally, once it reaches Alice's computer and you unwrap it,
然后最终，一旦它到达爱丽丝的电脑并且你将其解开，

1797
01:12:51,080 --> 01:12:54,080
you get specific applications on her computer.
你获取她电脑上的特定应用程序。

1798
01:12:54,080 --> 01:13:00,080
So it could be that Alice's Firefox application is talking to Bob's Google Chrome application,
所以可能是爱丽丝的火狐应用正在与鲍勃的谷歌浏览器应用进行通信，

1799
01:13:00,080 --> 01:13:07,080
or it could be the case that, you know, the zoom application on my computer is talking to the zoom application on your computer.
或者也可能是这样的情况，你知道，我电脑上的Zoom应用程序正在与你电脑上的Zoom应用程序进行通信。

1800
01:13:07,080 --> 01:13:13,080
So once we get to a specific computer, we can identify applications on the computer,
所以一旦我们接触到特定的计算机，我们就能识别出该计算机上的应用程序，

1801
01:13:13,080 --> 01:13:20,080
just like how once we reach a building, we can identify people inside the building by their room number or by their name.
正如我们到达一栋建筑后，可以通过房间号或姓名来识别楼内的人一样。

1802
01:13:20,080 --> 01:13:23,080
And then at the very inside, we have the original message.
而在最核心之处，我们拥有原始信息。

1803
01:13:23,080 --> 01:13:25,080
So that's kind of what it looks like.
大致上就是这个样子。

1804
01:13:25,080 --> 01:13:37,080
Question.
问。

1805
01:13:37,080 --> 01:13:38,080
Yeah, that's a great question.
是啊，这个问题提得真好。

1806
